## ❓ Essential Interview Questions

Q1: An employee calls the Helpdesk and says they cannot access the `\\DC01\Finance` shared drive. You can ping `192.168.1.50` successfully, but pinging `DC01` returns "host not found". What is the issue?
A1: The client machine has a DNS resolution failure. It is likely configured with an incorrect DNS server, such as a public Google DNS or a home router, preventing it from resolving internal Active Directory hostnames.

Q2: Why do we run `ipconfig /flushdns` before running `gpupdate /force` when fixing a network adapter?
A2: Windows caches DNS records to speed up browsing. If the cache still holds the broken or external routing information, Group Policy will fail to update. Flushing the cache forces the computer to immediately ask the Domain Controller for fresh, correct routing data.